  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Should You Repair or Replace a Damaged Bathroom Door Frame?",
    "text": "Should You Repair or Replace a Damaged Bathroom Door Frame?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Deciding whether to repair or replace a damaged bathroom door frame really depends on the extent and cause of the damage. It's not always an easy call, but HH Remodeling LLC can help you figure it out. First, you need to inspect the frame for what's actually going on. Is it just a few cosmetic dings or scratches? A simple repair like wood filler and a fresh coat of paint might be all you need. But if you're seeing visible rot, significant swelling, or the door itself isn't closing properly anymore, you're likely looking at more serious issues. A big red flag is if the damage is due to persistent moisture. If water has been getting into the frame for a while, there might be hidden rot or structural problems that a simple patch won't fix. You need to address the moisture source first, whether it's a leaky shower or just poor ventilation. Trying to patch over underlying water damage is a frequent mistake that just leads to the problem recurring. If the frame is wobbly, warped, or showing signs of structural compromise, a full replacement is usually the smarter, more long-term solution. This ensures the door will hang correctly and function safely. Ultimately, if the damage is more than superficial, or if you suspect hidden issues, it's definitely time to get a professional opinion. We can help you decide whether a careful repair or a complete replacement is the best path forward for your bathroom door frame, ensuring a lasting solution.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
}